WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.323
[MUSIC]

00:00:05.323 --> 00:00:07.562
I'm Julia Brown and I'm an introvert.

00:00:07.562 --> 00:00:10.060
I am shy.

00:00:10.060 --> 00:00:14.607
I'm Julia Brown and I'm an introvert.

00:00:14.607 --> 00:00:17.310
I have nothing to say.

00:00:17.310 --> 00:00:19.038
I'm Julia Brown [CROSSTALK].

00:00:19.038 --> 00:00:22.950
I'm Julia [CROSSTALK].

00:00:22.950 --> 00:00:30.396
I'm Julia Brown and

00:00:30.396 --> 00:00:37.847
I'm an introvert.

00:00:37.847 --> 00:00:38.470
And I love meeting new people.

00:00:40.700 --> 00:00:43.520
But at the end of the day, I need my time
to process,

00:00:43.520 --> 00:00:49.090
to parse out what I've learned and why
it's important.

00:00:49.090 --> 00:00:54.190
All my life, people have pushed me to be
somebody who I'm not.

00:00:54.190 --> 00:00:59.090
But I know that a smile from you, is all
the warmth and recognition that I need.

00:01:00.520 --> 00:01:02.630
In order to have this discussion today,

00:01:02.630 --> 00:01:06.810
I'd like you to remember that introversion
and extroversion are on a scale.

00:01:06.810 --> 00:01:09.145
We are all somewhere in between.

00:01:09.145 --> 00:01:12.580
45% of today's C suite executives, and

00:01:12.580 --> 00:01:15.680
over half the population identify as
introverts.

00:01:15.680 --> 00:01:17.380
But no one is 100% introverted or
extroverted.

00:01:20.180 --> 00:01:23.990
The word introvert literally means to turn
inward and

00:01:23.990 --> 00:01:27.100
that's exactly what introverts do.

00:01:27.100 --> 00:01:31.590
In order to process the day's events
introverts turn to the inner world

00:01:31.590 --> 00:01:35.800
of thought and feeling rather than living
in the moment.

00:01:35.800 --> 00:01:39.840
Introverts focus on the meaning of events,
and how that fits into the bigger picture.

00:01:40.960 --> 00:01:44.580
An introvert gains their energy through
reflection.

00:01:45.930 --> 00:01:49.000
I'm Julia Brown, and I'm an introvert and

00:01:49.000 --> 00:01:52.280
this is my story of breaking through the
noise.

00:01:53.780 --> 00:01:57.450
Imagine, you've just walked off a plane
and into a foreign country.

00:01:57.450 --> 00:02:00.880
It seems similar, but everything is
slightly different.

00:02:00.880 --> 00:02:02.290
The street signs.

00:02:02.290 --> 00:02:03.970
The smells of fried food and cigarettes.

00:02:05.000 --> 00:02:07.450
The sounds of traffic from the main
thoroughway, or

00:02:07.450 --> 00:02:09.810
children playing in a nearby schoolyard.

00:02:09.810 --> 00:02:12.110
Even the way the air feels sticky on your
skin.

00:02:13.720 --> 00:02:20.490
Being an introvert is like walking into a
foreign country everyday, where you,

00:02:20.490 --> 00:02:23.930
where all of your senses are heightened as
you try to find your balance.

00:02:25.190 --> 00:02:28.040
It's a rush and the feeling of
exhilaration and

00:02:28.040 --> 00:02:30.890
adventure bubble up inside of you.

00:02:30.890 --> 00:02:34.420
It's a puzzle that you're struggling to
figure out but

00:02:34.420 --> 00:02:37.440
all of the pieces are constantly moving
and changing.

00:02:38.630 --> 00:02:44.240
Over time you learn how it works, how it
fits together and what to expect.

00:02:45.950 --> 00:02:50.150
I feel that way every time I walk into a
room full of new people or

00:02:50.150 --> 00:02:52.730
have to deal with a new situation.

00:02:52.730 --> 00:02:56.750
But that's also how I survived walking off
a plane into Buenos Aries,

00:02:56.750 --> 00:02:59.910
Argentina, and apprenticing myself to a
chocolatier.

00:03:03.080 --> 00:03:08.170
Introverts have the amazing ability to
make their friends,

00:03:08.170 --> 00:03:11.150
acquaintances, and colleagues feel heard.

00:03:11.150 --> 00:03:16.155
Because they are listening, really closely
to what you have to say.

00:03:16.155 --> 00:03:18.560
They're trying to figure out what makes
you you.

00:03:18.560 --> 00:03:20.790
And why you do the things that you do.

00:03:20.790 --> 00:03:26.480
There's a reason, nerdy awkward Mark
Zuckerberg invented the social network.

00:03:26.480 --> 00:03:29.630
It's because he knew what you were going
to do before you did it yourself.

00:03:31.140 --> 00:03:33.050
I had studied Spanish in college.

00:03:33.050 --> 00:03:34.780
But nothing had prepared me for

00:03:34.780 --> 00:03:38.520
the rapid fire Spanish needed to work in
an Argentine kitchen.

00:03:38.520 --> 00:03:40.950
Being an introvert surprisingly worked in
my favor.

00:03:42.440 --> 00:03:47.480
By, by closely watching and working with
the people around me,

00:03:47.480 --> 00:03:50.910
I was able to learn much more quickly how
things should be done.

00:03:50.910 --> 00:03:55.950
How not to burn the chocolate, how long to
let the Ganache set for, and the delicate

00:03:55.950 --> 00:03:59.850
flick of the wrist needed to make a design
just so on the top of a truffle.

00:04:01.410 --> 00:04:05.940
Even in a fast-paced, loud kitchen, where
pans are clattering,

00:04:05.940 --> 00:04:10.080
the radio is blaring Mana, and people are
shouting from one end of the kitchen to

00:04:10.080 --> 00:04:15.170
the other, you as an introvert can connect
with people on a deep and

00:04:15.170 --> 00:04:17.780
personal level and break through the
noise.

00:04:19.570 --> 00:04:22.425
After I was a chocolatier I became a hedge
fund analyst.

00:04:22.425 --> 00:04:25.470
&gt;&gt; [LAUGH]
&gt;&gt; It's a little bit of a career non

00:04:25.470 --> 00:04:29.300
sequitur, I know, but it's almost the
perfect job for an introvert.

00:04:29.300 --> 00:04:33.300
You spend all day reading the news,
industry reports,

00:04:33.300 --> 00:04:36.520
interviewing experts and mom and pop
business owners.

00:04:36.520 --> 00:04:39.080
And then at the end of the day, you step
back and

00:04:39.080 --> 00:04:41.930
you distill that information into
investable ideas.

00:04:43.900 --> 00:04:46.820
But the world of investing is a world of
noise.

00:04:46.820 --> 00:04:49.420
The phones are constantly ringing.

00:04:49.420 --> 00:04:51.530
CNBC is blasting behind you and

00:04:51.530 --> 00:04:55.010
you feel as though you're living in a
perpetual earthquake

00:04:55.010 --> 00:05:00.110
where the next piece of news could shatter
the foundations of your investment thesis.

00:05:00.110 --> 00:05:00.790
Your ideas.

00:05:02.040 --> 00:05:06.080
The only way to survive in this world is
to have conviction.

00:05:06.080 --> 00:05:09.500
A belief so strong, it's interwoven with
your personality.

00:05:11.060 --> 00:05:16.500
Introverts are naturally analytical, by
taking the time to watch,

00:05:16.500 --> 00:05:18.660
listen, and process events.

00:05:18.660 --> 00:05:22.480
They can have contrarian unconventionals
or unconventional or

00:05:22.480 --> 00:05:23.939
even ahead of the curve ideas.

00:05:25.600 --> 00:05:28.770
But these same analytical tendencies

00:05:28.770 --> 00:05:33.040
force you to recognize just how fragile
your ideas are.

00:05:33.040 --> 00:05:37.650
You spend so much time thinking about your
ideas that their flaws and

00:05:37.650 --> 00:05:40.980
cracks are obvious to you and erode your
conviction.

00:05:43.150 --> 00:05:47.250
As an introvert you have to fight this
tendency to turn inward.

00:05:47.250 --> 00:05:51.330
To write off your ideas because of their
imperfections.

00:05:51.330 --> 00:05:53.850
As an introvert, you have to make yourself
vulnerable.

00:05:55.140 --> 00:05:59.360
These ideas, that ones that are integral
to who we are,

00:05:59.360 --> 00:06:01.240
are the ones we need to share with the
world.

00:06:02.840 --> 00:06:04.410
The returns are worth the risks.

00:06:06.440 --> 00:06:10.760
Warren Buffett was a 25 year old no name
kid who couldn't get a job.

00:06:10.760 --> 00:06:13.210
So he started his own investment firm.

00:06:13.210 --> 00:06:16.580
He bought companies where nobody else saw
value.

00:06:16.580 --> 00:06:18.895
Today, he's the greatest investor of our
time.

00:06:18.895 --> 00:06:22.060
Mr. Buffett is a self-described introvert.

00:06:23.570 --> 00:06:27.060
I started working at a hedge fund as a 25
year old no name kid

00:06:27.060 --> 00:06:28.510
as a part time office manager.

00:06:29.930 --> 00:06:32.540
Within three years I was a full time
analyst and

00:06:32.540 --> 00:06:37.500
two of the ideas I had worked on were our
two biggest returns in the fund.

00:06:37.500 --> 00:06:42.350
I'm not saying I'm the next Warren Buffet
but I do know that

00:06:42.350 --> 00:06:45.870
having conviction means knowing where the
limits of your belief system are.

00:06:46.870 --> 00:06:50.420
I know which events can render my ideas
useless and

00:06:50.420 --> 00:06:53.080
I can quantify that downside for you.

00:06:53.080 --> 00:06:55.950
But by knowing how large that downside is

00:06:55.950 --> 00:06:58.800
I also know by how much the returns
outweigh that risk.

00:07:00.040 --> 00:07:03.920
Having conviction means knowing that you
might fail but

00:07:03.920 --> 00:07:06.100
how much better it will be if you succeed.

00:07:07.430 --> 00:07:13.080
Know your ideas, be unconventional, break
through the noise.

00:07:15.060 --> 00:07:18.880
At this point, you're probably saying to
yourself, I've heard all of this before.

00:07:18.880 --> 00:07:22.680
I know it, but how do I actually get
anyone to notice?

00:07:22.680 --> 00:07:23.540
How do I speak up?

00:07:24.600 --> 00:07:29.720
It is impossible to break through the
noise without speaking up.

00:07:29.720 --> 00:07:31.610
Believe me, I've tried every way.

00:07:33.650 --> 00:07:36.060
And it's something I still struggle with
today.

00:07:36.060 --> 00:07:40.430
Which is why I am here on a stage in a
room full of people.

00:07:42.250 --> 00:07:45.910
Every day I struggle to break through the
noise of my own self doubt.

00:07:47.360 --> 00:07:52.420
Luckily, I've had my own champions, my
family, friends, and

00:07:52.420 --> 00:07:57.890
mentors, who were able to break through my
quiet and

00:07:57.890 --> 00:08:01.500
protected facade, and find something that
they too believed in.

00:08:03.270 --> 00:08:08.950
These people have paved the way for me to
make some seemingly crazy choices that

00:08:08.950 --> 00:08:10.880
turned out to be the best decisions of my
life.

00:08:12.680 --> 00:08:16.780
These people pull me out of my own
protective cone of silence and

00:08:16.780 --> 00:08:20.450
give me the strength to keep trying when
everything seems impossible.

00:08:22.320 --> 00:08:24.140
Find your champions.

00:08:24.140 --> 00:08:27.490
They will give you the power to break
through the noise.

00:08:29.510 --> 00:08:36.430
In a world that is constantly asking you
to speak up, to make yourself vulnerable,

00:08:36.430 --> 00:08:43.050
to make yourself heard, sometimes breaking
through the noise seems hard.

00:08:43.050 --> 00:08:47.837
But it is the perfect opportunity to rise
to the occasion and challenge yourself.

00:08:49.000 --> 00:08:53.000
Taking this risk becomes so much easier if
you value yourself.

00:08:54.340 --> 00:08:55.040
Know your skills.

00:08:56.420 --> 00:09:00.670
You have the incredible ability to make
people feel heard

00:09:00.670 --> 00:09:03.830
in a world where that's all anyone around
you is asking for.

00:09:05.250 --> 00:09:09.150
And do you have the ability to come up
with creative,

00:09:09.150 --> 00:09:13.184
outside of the box ideas that can shatter
the limits of the world that we live in?

00:09:13.184 --> 00:09:15.520
Know yourself.

00:09:15.520 --> 00:09:18.826
Challenge yourself.

00:09:18.826 --> 00:09:21.360
Trust yourself.

00:09:21.360 --> 00:09:23.086
Break through the noise.

00:09:23.086 --> 00:09:25.346
Thank you.

00:09:25.346 --> 00:09:26.737
[APPLAUSE]

00:09:26.737 --> 00:09:31.259
[MUSIC]

